partialText:
&lt;p&gt;You're building a webhook handler. It runs on &lt;code&gt;localhost:3000&lt;/code&gt;. GitHub needs a public HTTPS address to send to, so the delivery never arrives, and you're writing your handler against the JSON sample in the docs instead of what GitHub really sends.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Here's a way to get the real delivery onto your machine, headers and body intact, without a tunnel and without installing anything.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  1. Get a public address that records everything
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Open &lt;a href="https://curler.dev" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;curler.dev&lt;/a&gt; and click &lt;strong&gt;Create a bin&lt;/strong&gt;. The top bar shows a capture URL like:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;https://api.curler.dev/h/fZU_aI73r6LZkEr4eThskAPiWwXaXa
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Anything sent to that address, or to any path below it, is recorded: method, path, headers and the raw body.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  2. Point GitHub at it
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;In your repository, open &lt;strong&gt;Settings → Webhooks → Add webhook&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Payload URL:&lt;/strong&gt; the capture URL, plus a path if your handler uses one, for example &lt;code&gt;https://api.curler.dev/h/&amp;lt;your-bin&amp;gt;/webhooks/github&lt;/code&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Content type:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;code&gt;application/json&lt;/code&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Secret:&lt;/strong&gt; the same secret your handler checks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Save, then push a commit. The delivery shows up in the bin within a couple of seconds. Click it to see every header GitHub sent (&lt;code&gt;X-GitHub-Event&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;X-GitHub-Delivery&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;X-Hub-Signature-256&lt;/code&gt;) and the body as a JSON tree.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  3. Replay it against localhost
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Under the request, set &lt;strong&gt;replay target&lt;/strong&gt; to your app's address, for example &lt;code&gt;http://localhost:3000&lt;/code&gt;, and copy the Bash command. It comes as one line; here it is shortened and wrapped for reading:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight shell"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="nb"&gt;printf&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'%s'&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'{"ref":"refs/heads/main","repository":{"full_name":"octo/demo"},...}'&lt;/span&gt; \
  &lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; curl --globoff -X &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'POST'&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'http://localhost:3000/webhooks/github'&lt;/span&gt; \
    -H &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'User-Agent: GitHub-Hookshot/…'&lt;/span&gt; \
    -H &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'Content-Type: application/json'&lt;/span&gt; \
    -H &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'X-Github-Delivery: 72d3162e-cc78-11e3-81ab-4c9367dc0958'&lt;/span&gt; \
    -H &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'X-Github-Event: push'&lt;/span&gt; \
    -H &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'X-Hub-Signature-256: sha256=…'&lt;/span&gt; \
    --data-binary @-
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Paste it in a terminal and your handler receives the same request GitHub sent. Run it again as often as you like while you fix your code: set a breakpoint, change a line, replay.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;There's a PowerShell version next to it for Windows.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Why the body has to be byte for byte
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;GitHub signs the raw body with your secret, and your handler checks &lt;code&gt;X-Hub-Signature-256&lt;/code&gt; against the bytes it receives. One changed space, a re-ordered key or a different line ending, and the check fails.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Curler stores the body exactly as it arrived, and the copied command sends it back byte for byte. A binary body goes through base64 so the shell can't alter it. So the signature check in your handler passes on a replay, exactly as it would on a live delivery.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  When it's not GitHub
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The same steps work for any sender that needs a public URL: Stripe, Shopify, Slack, or the callback of an SSO provider such as Okta or Auth0. For a login callback, Curler shows you the exact query string or form post the provider sent, which is usually where the reason for a failed login hides.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Good to know
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Curler is free: a bin lives 24 hours and keeps its newest 100 requests.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The bin's page updates on its own while it's open, so you can leave it next to your editor.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Curler's server sleeps when nobody uses it, and the first call after a quiet spell can take about 10 seconds. GitHub waits 10 seconds for an answer, so open your bin's page before you trigger the first delivery. If one is missed, &lt;strong&gt;Redeliver&lt;/strong&gt; on GitHub's webhook page sends it again.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Captured content is never rendered as HTML, so a hostile payload can't run in your browser.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I'm the developer of Curler. If something about your webhook didn't show up the way you expected, tell me: &lt;a href="mailto:feedback@curler.dev"&gt;feedback@curler.dev&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h1&gt;


  Automating Multi‑Channel Content Metadata Sync in a Next.js Monorepo
&lt;/h1&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;TL;DR:&lt;/strong&gt; I added a post‑publish hook that writes the newly generated Bluesky URIs and the Dev.to article URL back into the central &lt;code&gt;metadata.json&lt;/code&gt; files. This keeps all channel metadata in sync automatically and eliminates manual copy‑paste errors.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


  The Problem
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Our content‑automation pipeline generates Markdown for Medium, Substack and Bluesky, then publishes each piece via separate scripts. After each successful publish we need to store the resulting identifiers (Bluesky AT‑URIs, Dev.to article URL, etc.) so that later jobs—like newsletter generation or SEO audits—can reference them.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The metadata lives in &lt;code&gt;content/&amp;lt;date&amp;gt;/&amp;lt;project&amp;gt;/metadata.json&lt;/code&gt;. Before this change the file was edited manually after each publish. The symptom was obvious:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight json"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="err"&gt;$&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;cat&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;content&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="err"&gt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;2026&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="err"&gt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;11&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="err"&gt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;09&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="err"&gt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;content&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="err"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;automation&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="err"&gt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;metadata&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="err"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;json&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="err"&gt;...&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"bluesky_uris"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nl"&gt;"es"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"at://did:plc:y5omxao2h2bnmixo7sigikex/app.bsky.feed.post/3mzw7dtidwa2j"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"at://did:plc:y5omxao2h2bnmi"&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"devto_url"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;""&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The &lt;code&gt;devto_url&lt;/code&gt; stayed empty because I forgot to paste it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The &lt;code&gt;bluesky_uris.es&lt;/code&gt; array sometimes contained duplicate URIs after a retry, causing downstream scripts to process the same post twice.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Every time a new channel was added we had to remember to edit the JSON manually, which is error‑prone and hard to audit.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


  What I Tried First
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;My first attempt was a quick &lt;code&gt;fs.appendFile&lt;/code&gt; in the &lt;code&gt;scripts/publish-bluesky.ts&lt;/code&gt; script:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// scripts/publish-bluesky.ts (initial version)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;promises&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;as&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;fs&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'fs'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;publishToBluesky&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'../src/lib/bluesky'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;async&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;main&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;uri&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;publishToBluesky&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;'content/2026/11/09/content-automation/bluesky_en.json'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;fs&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;appendFile&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'content/2026/11/09/content-automation/metadata.json'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="sb"&gt;`"${uri}",\n`&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;main&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;I ran the script twice (once for English, once for Spanish) and ended up with duplicated entries in the &lt;code&gt;es&lt;/code&gt; array. The file also lost its proper JSON structure because I was appending raw text. The error manifested as a JSON parse failure in the next step of the pipeline:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;SyntaxError: Unexpected token } in JSON at position 342
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;






&lt;h2&gt;


  The Implementation
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  1. Define a Typed Metadata Model
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I created a small TypeScript interface to describe the shape of &lt;code&gt;metadata.json&lt;/code&gt;. This lives in &lt;code&gt;src/types/metadata.ts&lt;/code&gt;:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// src/types/metadata.ts&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;interface&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Metadata&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="n"&gt;bluesky_published&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;boolean&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="n"&gt;bluesky_uris&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;en&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;es&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="n"&gt;devto_url&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Having a type forces the compiler to catch structural mistakes early.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  2. Idempotent Update Helper
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The core of the solution is &lt;code&gt;src/lib/metadata.ts&lt;/code&gt;. It reads the file, merges new URIs without duplication, and writes the file back atomically.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// src/lib/metadata.ts&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;promises&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;as&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;fs&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'fs'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;join&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'path'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Metadata&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'../types/metadata'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="no"&gt;METADATA_ROOT&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'content/2026/11/09'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;async&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;updateMetadata&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="n"&gt;project&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;newBlueskyUri&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;lang&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;devtoUrl&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;newBlueskyUri&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;?:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;lang&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;?:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'en'&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'es'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;devtoUrl&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;?:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;path&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;join&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="no"&gt;METADATA_ROOT&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;project&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'metadata.json'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;raw&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;fs&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;readFile&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;path&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'utf-8'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Metadata&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;JSON&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;parse&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;raw&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Merge Bluesky URIs idempotently&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;newBlueskyUri&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;amp;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;lang&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;set&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;Set&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;bluesky_uris&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;lang&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;set&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;add&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;newBlueskyUri&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;bluesky_uris&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;lang&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;Array&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;set&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;bluesky_published&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Update Dev.to URL once&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;devtoUrl&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;devto_url&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;devtoUrl&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Write back with 2‑space indentation&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;fs&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;writeFile&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;path&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;JSON&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;stringify&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;null&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;2&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Key points:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Set&lt;/strong&gt; guarantees uniqueness, preventing the duplicate‑URI bug we saw earlier.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The function is &lt;strong&gt;purely functional&lt;/strong&gt;: it does not assume any global state.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Writing with &lt;code&gt;JSON.stringify(..., null, 2)&lt;/code&gt; keeps the file human‑readable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

